          "content": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>dsh vs Claude Code</title>\n<style>\n  :root { --bg: #fff; --fg: #1a1a1a; --muted: #6b6b6b; --line: #e6e6e6; --good: #1a7f37; --bad: #b42318; }\n  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {\n    :root { --bg: #141414; --fg: #e8e8e8; --muted: #9a9a9a; --line: #2a2a2a; --good: #4ac26b; --bad: #f97066; }\n  }\n  body { background: var(--bg); color: var(--fg); font: 15px/1.6 system-ui, -apple-system, \"Segoe UI\", sans-serif; margin: 0; }\n  main { max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 48px 16px 64px; }\n  h1 { font-size: 24px; font-weight: 600; margin: 0 0 4px; }\n  h2 { font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .06em; color: var(--muted); margin: 40px 0 12px; }\n  p, li { margin: 0 0 8px; }\n  ul { padding-left: 20px; margin: 0; }\n  .sub { color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 32px; }\n  .verdict { border-left: 3px solid var(--fg); padding: 4px 0 4px 16px; font-size: 16px; }\n  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }\n  th, td { text-align: left; padding: 8px 8px 8px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }\n  th { font-weight: 500; color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; }\n  .pass { color: var(--good); }\n  .fail { color: var(--bad); }\n  code { font: 13px ui-monospace, Consolas, monospace; }\n  .wrap { overflow-x: auto; }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<main>\n  <h1>dsh vs Claude Code</h1>\n  <p class=\"sub\">File-finding eval · 7–8 Oct 2026 · same model for both: <code>lynx harness</code> via OmniRoute (gemini-3.7-flash-high)</p>\n\n  <div class=\"verdict\">\n    Both agents find the right files equally well. Claude Code still wins overall: it finished every task,\n    while dsh lost two runs to gateway errors and used more steps and tokens. The gateway issue is now fixed in dsh.\n  </div>\n\n  <h2>Results</h2>\n  <div class=\"wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <tr><th>Task</th><th>dsh</th><th>Claude Code</th></tr>\n    <tr><td>f04ad05f30</td><td class=\"pass\">Pass · 38 steps</td><td class=\"pass\">Pass · 20 steps</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>ed34a1d7fe</td><td class=\"pass\">Pass · 55 steps</td><td class=\"pass\">Pass · 39 steps</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>a59beb8ae3</td><td class=\"pass\">Pass · 49 steps</td><td class=\"pass\">Pass · 51 steps</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>9633724b40</td><td class=\"pass\">Pass · 98 steps</td><td class=\"pass\">Pass · 79 steps</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>980b410340</td><td class=\"fail\">Error · gateway 502</td><td class=\"pass\">Pass</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>4b9d8ad6f7</td><td class=\"fail\">Error · gateway 504</td><td class=\"pass\">Pass</td></tr>\n  </table>\n  </div>\n  <p style=\"margin-top:12px;color:var(--muted)\">Two more tasks (54fa38795f, e21ed97f29) were left out: they can't be tested on Windows here.</p>\n\n  <h2>Where each one stands</h2>\n  <ul>\n    <li><b>Finding files: tie.</b> Step where the right file was first seen: dsh 2, 3, 3, 2 · Claude Code 4, 3, 2, 1.</li>\n    <li><b>Steps: Claude Code better.</b> 189 vs 240 steps on the four tasks both passed (dsh used about 27% more).</li>\n    <li><b>Cost: Claude Code better.</b> 563K vs 782K input tokens on three tasks (dsh used about 39% more).</li>\n    <li><b>Surviving gateway errors: Claude Code better.</b> Both lost dsh runs failed on gateway errors, not wrong answers.</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h2>Why dsh lost two runs</h2>\n  <ul>\n    <li><b>980b410340:</b> OmniRoute sent a 502. The error text listed IPv6 addresses like <code>2001:4860:4844:400::</code>,\n      and dsh read that “400” as “bad request, don't retry”. It stopped without retrying once.</li>\n    <li><b>4b9d8ad6f7:</b> dsh retried 5 times with waits capped at 10 s. It gave up at 07:47 UTC.\n      The gateway was working again by 07:51.</li>\n    <li><b>Claude Code</b> hit the same kinds of errors (504 at 08:00; a 502 and four 503s at 08:22)\n      and got through both times by retrying longer.</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h2>What was fixed</h2>\n  <ul>\n    <li><b>Error reading:</b> a number now only counts as a status code if it stands alone, not inside an address.\n      Fix in <code>llm-pi-ai/src/stream.ts</code>; the real error from that run is now a test.</li>\n    <li><b>Retry settings now match Claude Code:</b> 10 retries instead of 5; longest wait 32 s instead of 10 s.\n      These are the values in Claude Code's own install. dsh now keeps trying for about 2.5 minutes instead of about 15 seconds.\n      Fix in <code>llm/src/retry-policy.ts</code>.</li>\n    <li><b>Checks:</b> type-check and lint clean · 1066 tests pass · the 7 deepseek-adapter tests that fail\n      were already failing before these changes (they expect model names like “deepseek-V4-Pro” but the renamed code says “Lynx-V4-Pro”).</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h2>Still open</h2>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Not yet proven in a real run that the retry fix saves a run like 4b9d8ad6f7. It will show the next time the gateway fails.</li>\n    <li>dsh's extra steps and tokens are the main gap left. The next step is to measure where the extra context comes from.</li>\n    <li>Nothing is committed yet.</li>\n    <li>Claude Code installed VS Build Tools (about 1.6 GB) during the eval. You can uninstall it from Windows Settings.</li>\n  </ul>\n</main>\n</body>\n</html>\n"
